                    AwakeningSection(heading: "How to Tell Light from Dark — In Real Time", body: "You've studied the theory. Now the practical tool.\n\nThis builds on ERSS (Module 12 of Journeys of Awakening) but applies specifically to spiritual, religious, and consciousness claims. Because some of the most dangerous deceptions in human history have worn spiritual clothing.\n\nTHE LIGHT/DARK DISCERNMENT PROTOCOL\n\nFor any teaching, teacher, tradition, practice, or claim — run these 7 tests:\n\n1. THE UNITY TEST\nDoes it UNITE or DIVIDE?\nLight unites. Darkness divides. Always. If a teaching requires you to hate, fear, or dehumanize a group — it's dark, regardless of what name it operates under. If it says \"WE are chosen and THEY are damned\" — red flag. Every genuine tradition's highest teaching points toward unity: \"Love your neighbor\" (Christianity), \"All beings\" (Buddhism), \"Humanity is one family\" (Islam), \"We are fractals of the whole\" (SunFlow).\n\n2. THE FREEDOM TEST\nDoes it LIBERATE or CONTROL?\nLight expands your choices. Darkness narrows them. If a teaching demands obedience through fear (\"believe this or burn\"), punishes questioning, isolates you from other perspectives, or claims to be the ONLY source of truth — it's operating in control mode. Genuine light invites examination. Counterfeit light forbids it.\n\n3. THE FRUIT TEST\nWhat does it PRODUCE in practitioners?\nJesus: \"By their fruits you will know them\" (Matthew 7:16). Do the people who follow this path become more loving, more honest, more compassionate, more free? Or more fearful, more judgmental, more rigid, more isolated? The teaching's truth is proven by its effect, not its claims.\n\n4. THE TRANSPARENCY TEST\nDoes it WELCOME or FEAR scrutiny?\nLight doesn't need to hide. If a teacher, organization, or tradition punishes investigation, suppresses internal criticism, or uses spiritual authority to silence dissent — the structure is dark, even if the original teaching was light.\n\n5. THE SACRIFICE TEST\nWHO sacrifices and WHO benefits?\nLight asks the leader to sacrifice for the people. Darkness asks the people to sacrifice for the leader. Every cult inverts this. Every false god demands your children, your money, your autonomy. The genuine path asks you to sacrifice ego — and gives back freedom.\n\n6. THE FEAR TEST\nIs the primary motivator LOVE or FEAR?\nLight draws through love, beauty, truth. Darkness drives through fear, shame, guilt. If the first thing a teaching does is make you afraid — of hell, of punishment, of rejection, of cosmic forces — before it makes you feel loved, valued, and empowered — reverse the sequence. Love first. Always.\n\n7. THE EGO TEST\nDoes it DISSOLVE ego or INFLATE ego?\nLight: \"You are part of something infinitely greater than yourself.\" Dark: \"You are special, chosen, superior.\" Spiritual ego is the final and most dangerous false god — the ego that thinks it's enlightened. If a teaching makes you feel better THAN others rather than connected TO others — it's feeding the wrong thing."),
                    AwakeningSection(heading: "Applying the Protocol", body: "RUN IT ON EVERYTHING.\n\nRun it on Christianity. Run it on Buddhism. Run it on New Age. Run it on SunFlow. Run it on this very course.\n\nNothing gets a pass. If it's genuinely light, it will WELCOME the examination and score well. If it fails the tests, you have information — regardless of how prestigious, ancient, or popular the source.\n\nPRACTICE EXERCISE 1: Pick a spiritual teaching you currently follow.\nScore it 1-10 on each test (Unity, Freedom, Fruit, Transparency, Sacrifice, Fear, Ego).\nTotal range: 7-70.\n• 50-70: Strongly aligned with light\n• 30-49: Mixed — elements of both, investigate further\n• 7-29: More darkness than light in its CURRENT expression (note: even genuine traditions can be corrupted by human institutions)\n\nPRACTICE EXERCISE 2: Pick a spiritual teaching you REJECT.\nScore it the same way. You might be surprised. Sometimes what we reject scores higher than what we accept — because our rejection was inherited, not examined.\n\nPRACTICE EXERCISE 3: Score yourself.\nNot a tradition — YOU. Your current way of moving through the world.\n• Do your actions unite or divide?\n• Do you liberate or control the people around you?\n• What fruit does your life produce?\n• Do you welcome scrutiny or get defensive?\n• Are you motivated more by love or fear?\n• Is your ego growing or dissolving?\n\nThis is the hardest test. And the most important one. Because you can study every tradition in history and still be running darkness in your own operating system without realizing it.\n\nThe curriculum isn't just about KNOWING light from dark. It's about BECOMING someone who consistently chooses and generates light. That's the inner work. That's the shadow work. That's the whole point."),
